    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0175" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/316a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Representatives in Great Britain, France,
                            Russia, Italy, and Japan
                    </hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d1-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Press this morning publishes report that President will send second note to
                    powers in effort to advance peace movement. You may say that this report is
                    utterly false and without foundation and that the President has not in
                    contemplation sending a second note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d1-f1-content">
                <p>The same, on the same date, to the Ambassadors in Germany, Austria-Hungary, and
                    Turkey, except that the second sentence begins, “If inquiry made you may reply,”
                    instead of “You may say” (File No. 763.72119/325a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
